same dataset,\n> but only belong to the same series if all their categories except `reference_date`\n> are **exactly** the same.\n\nAs the number of series may be large, the response may be divided into several pages.\nThe next page can be obtained by specifying the `page=n` query string parameter\n(where _n_ is the page number, starting at 1). The presence of an `extension` / `next_page`\nattribute (containing the link for the next page) indicates a multi-page response.\n\nEach page is guaranteed to contain all requested observations for a particular series.\nIn other words, pages are never split mid-series and should be consumed as separate\n**[JSON-stat datasets](https://json-stat.org/format/#class)**.\n\nThe set of categories returned in each page are only the categories that apply to the\nseries contained in that particular page, not the full set of categories for all series\ncontained in the dataset.\n\n**Example:**\n\n```\n$ curl -sSL -X GET 'https://bpstat.bportugal.pt/data/v1/domains/59/datasets/b8cc662879c9f7b0f3faf89c7871fc38/?lang=EN&series_ids=167795'\n```", "parameters": [{"name": "domain_id", "in": "path", "description": "Domain ID.", "type": "integer", "required": true}, {"name": "dataset_id", "in": "path", "description": "Dataset ID.", "type": "string", "required": true}, {"name": "series_ids", "in": "query", "description": "Comma-separated list of series IDs (ex: `1` or `1,2,3`).\n\nSelect only observations from these particular series.", "type": "string"}, {"name": "lang", "in": "query", "description": "Language for entity descriptions, one of: \n* `PT` &mdash; portuguese\n* `EN` &mdash; english", "type": "string", "default": "PT"}, {"name": "decimal", "in": "query", "description": "Return values as fixed-point decimals rather than floating-point.\n\nBy default observation values are returned as `float` to make them easier to use in analysis tools. If you prefer to get the values with the exact same number of decimal places as displayed in the BPstat website, use `decimal=true`.", "type": "string", "default": false}, {"name": "recurrence", "in": "query", "description": "Observation interval, one of: \n* `A` &mdash; annual\n* `S` &mdash; biannual\n* `T` &mdash; quarterly\n* `M` &mdash; monthly\n* `D` &mdash; daily", "type": "string"}, {"name": "dim_cats", "in": "query", "description": "Filter by these categories, as a comma-separated list of `dimension_id:category_id` pairs.", "type": "string"}, {"name": "obs_since", "in": "query", "description": "Restrict to observations with reference dates strictly at and before this date.", "type": "string", "format": "date"}, {"name": "obs_to", "in": "query", "description": "Restrict to observations with reference dates at and after this date.", "type": "string", "format": "date"}, {"name": "obs_published_since", "in": "query", "description": "Restrict to observations **published** at and after this time (in `iso-8601` format).", "type": "string", "format": "date-time"}, {"name": "obs_last_n", "in": "query", "description": "Restrict to the most recent _n_ observations.", "type": "integer"}, {"name": "page", "in": "query", "description": "Fetch this page number (when more than one page).", "type": "integer", "default": 1}, {"name": "page_size", "in": "query", "description": "Maximum number of objects in (paginated) response.", "type": "integer", "default": 10}], "responses": {"200": {"description": "", "schema": {"$ref": "#/definitions/Dataset"}}}, "tags": ["API Methods"]}, "parameters": [{"name": "domain_id", "in": "path", "required": true, "type": "string"}, {"name": "dataset_id", "in": "path", "required": true, "type": "string"}]}, "/data/v1/domains/{domain_id}/dimensions/": {"get": {"operationId": "domain_dimensions", "summary": "List Domain Dimensions", "description": "Lists all available **dimensions** for the specified statistical domain.\n\nThis set of dimensions constitutes the union of all dimensions available across every dataset\ncontained in the domain, and each dataset will use just a (unique) subset of them.\n\nThe dimension `id`s can be found inside the `extension` dictionary of each collection `item`, and may\nbe used to filter the [list of datasets](#operation/domain_datasets) contained in the domain.\n\nAs the number of dimensions may be large, the response may be divided into several pages.\nThe next page can be obtained by specifying the `page=n` query string parameter\n(where _n_ is the page number, starting at 1). The presence of an `extension` / `next_page`\nattribute (containing the link for the next page) indicates a multi-page response.\n\nEach page should be consumed as a separate **[JSON-stat collection](https://json-stat.org/format/#class)**.\n\n**Example:**\n\n```\n$ curl -sSL -X GET 'https://bpstat.bportugal.pt/data/v1/domains/59/dimensions/?lang=EN'\n```", "parameters": [{"name": "domain_id", "in": "path", "description": "Domain ID.", "type": "integer", "required": true}, {"name": "lang", "in": "query", "description": "Language for entity descriptions, one of: \n* `PT` &mdash; portuguese\n* `EN` &mdash; english", "type": "string", "default": "PT"}, {"name": "page", "in": "query", "description": "Fetch this page number (when more than one page).", "type": "integer", "default": 1}, {"name": "page_size", "in": "query", "description": "Maximum number of objects in (paginated) response.", "type": "integer", "default": 10}], "responses": {"200": {"description": "", "schema": {"$ref": "#/definitions/DimensionCollection"}}}, "tags": ["API Methods"]}, "parameters": [{"name": "domain_id", "in": "path", "required": true, "type": "string"}]}, "/data/v1/domains/{domain_id}/dimensions/{dimension_id}/": {"get": {"operationId": "domain_dimension_detail", "summary": "List Dimension Categories", "description": "Returns the details for the specified **dimension**, including its label and all the categories contained in it.\n\nThe response can be consumed as a **[JSON-stat dimension](https://json-stat.org/format/#class)**.\n\n**Example:**\n\n```\n$ curl -sSL -X GET 'https://bpstat.bportugal.pt/data/v1/domains/59/dimensions/63/?lang=EN'\n```", "parameters": [{"name": "domain_id", "in": "path", "description": "Domain ID.", "type": "integer", "required": true}, {"name": "dimension_id", "in": "path", "description": "Dimension ID.", "type": "integer", "required": true}, {"name": "lang", "in": "query", "description": "Language for entity descriptions, one of: \n* `PT` &mdash; portuguese\n* `EN` &mdash; english", "type": "string", "default": "PT"}], "responses": {"200": {"description": "", "schema": {"$ref": "#/definitions/Dimension"}}}, "tags": ["API Methods"]}, "parameters": [{"name": "domain_id", "in": "path", "required": true, "type": "string"}, {"name": "dimension_id", "in": "path", "required": true, "type": "string"}]}, "/data/v1/series/": {"get": {"operationId": "series", "summary": "List Series Details", "description": "Returns detailed information about the list of series specified in the `series_ids` query string parameter.\n\nThis information includes the ID of the dataset containing observations for the series and the ID(s) for the\nstatistical domain(s) where they are present. These IDs can then be used to retrieve observations using the\n[Get Dataset](#operation/domain_dataset_detail) operation (perhaps filtered using the same list of series).\n\nIt also includes the structure of the series (their dimensions and specific categories that define them), which\ncan also be used to filter a [dataset](#operation/domain_dataset_detail) and obtain just series related by\nsome subset of dimensions and categories (e.g. series that vary only by territory, or only by recurrence, or both).\n\nSeries that don't exist are simply omitted from the response, which may result in an empty list\nif none of the series exist.\n\n**Example:**\n\n```\n$ curl -sSL -X GET 'https://bpstat.bportugal.pt/data/v1/series/?lang=EN&series_ids=167795,167791'\n```", "parameters": [{"name": "series_ids", "in": 